   "summary": "Shiga describes his family, schooling in Hagi, participation in a rice riot, and political reading before entering the First Higher School and Tokyo Imperial University. He recounts organizing students and the early Communist movement, then his arrest in the March 15 roundup and efforts to sustain morale and communication in prison. He criticizes comrades who divulged information or renounced the party, and describes the 1931 trial, public support, unequal treatment of defendants, and beatings after court. The account continues beyond page 108.",
